<title>USA: National City to merge with Bridgeport.</title>
<headline>National City to merge with Bridgeport.</headline>
<dateline>EVANSVILLE, Ind. 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>National City Bancshares Inc, a multi-bank holding company, said Monday it reached a merger agreement with Bridgeport Bancorp Inc, a one- bank holding company for First National Bank of Bridgeport, Ill.</p>
<p>Terms were not disclosed.</p>
<p>The transaction, which must be approved by regulators, will increase National City's total consolidated assets to about $1.2 billion. First National Bank had total assets of $40 million as of March 31, 1997.</p>
<p>((Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
